        "intro_screen_title": "Learn Tamil Letters and their Sounds",
        "intro_screen": [
            {
                "sub_title": "Independent Vowels (உயிர் எழுத்துகள்)",
                "description": "In Tamil, vowels are called உயிர் எழுத்துகள் (Uyir Ezhuthukal). They are the basic sounds of the language and can be written independently. Tamil has 12 independent vowels: அ, ஆ, இ, ஈ, உ, ஊ, எ, ஏ, ஐ, ஒ, ஓ, ஔ. These vowels form the foundation of Tamil script and pronunciation, with each having its unique sound and form. Tamil vowels are categorized into short vowels (குறில்) and long vowels (நெடில்)."
